# ShellCheck policy for the HADA repository.
# Consumed automatically by the `shellcheck` invocations in
# .github/workflows/verify.yml ("Check shell scripts") and local runs.
#
# Each disabled code below is a documented structural false positive for
# this repository's layout, NOT a blanket relaxation. Genuine defect
# classes (quoting, word-splitting, SC2124, SC2115, SC2155, etc.) remain
# enforced at their default levels.
#
# SC2034 (unused variable): the Phase B test harness assigns configuration
#   variables (SSH_CMD, CREATED_CONTAINERS, UNIT_INSTALLED, ...) and then
#   `source`s workspace/scripts/run-phase-b-deploy.sh, which consumes them
#   in the same shell. ShellCheck cannot see across `source` boundaries
#   here, so it reports every such variable as unused.
# SC1091 (not following sourced file): same `source` pattern; the sourced
#   paths are computed at runtime (${RUNNER}, ${HERE}/lib_mock_remote.sh,
#   /etc/os-release on target hosts) and cannot be resolved statically.
# SC2317 (unreachable command): cleanup/summary functions are invoked only
#   via `trap ... EXIT`, which ShellCheck flags as unreachable.
# SC2016 (expressions don't expand in single quotes): single quotes are
#   deliberate — remote commands passed to `bash -c` / ssh must expand on
#   the remote side, and grep patterns intentionally match literal `${...}`.
# SC2015 (A && B || C): the assert_pass/assert_fail chains use this form
#   deliberately; assert_pass never fails, so the caveat does not apply.
# SC2329 (function never invoked): helper functions are called indirectly
#   (traps, sourced consumers).
# SC2002 (useless cat): style-only.
disable=SC2034,SC1091,SC2317,SC2016,SC2015,SC2329,SC2002
